  "steps": [
    "Soak the dried porcini in 200ml of the hot stock for 10 minutes, then lift out, chop, and keep the soaking liquid.",
    "Sweat the onion in olive oil over medium-low heat until soft, then add garlic and the fresh mushrooms. Cook until golden, about 8 minutes.",
    "Stir in the rice and toast for two minutes until the edges look glassy. Pour in the wine and let it bubble away.",
    "Add the stock a ladleful at a time, stirring often, waiting until each addition is absorbed before the next. Include the porcini and their liquid.",
    "After 18–20 minutes the rice should be creamy with a slight bite. Beat in the vegan butter and nutritional yeast.",
    "Rest off the heat for two minutes, then scatter with parsley and serve at once."
  ],
  "notes": "Keep your stock simmering on a back burner — adding cold stock shocks the rice and slows the cook. A squeeze of lemon at the end lifts everything."
}
